<file path="CHANGELOG.md">
# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [0.0.4.5.10] - 2026-10-24

### Added
- REA Stdio Transport: Built-in on-demand stdio child-process execution (`node rea.mjs --mcp`) in `runtime/capability-engine.ts`, eliminating the requirement for standing background HTTP daemons.
- Live Capability Probe & Invocation: Automated discovery via `probeLocalReaTools()` and execution via `executeReaViaStdio()`, verified against real local targets (`whoami.exe`) and 207 discovered MCP operations.
- REA End-to-End Integration Test: `runtime/rea-stdio-integration.test.cjs` covering full Intake Gate, capability selection, tool execution, evidence capture, non-REA isolation, and fail-closed permission enforcement.

### Changed
- Transitioned version identity to `0.0.4.5.10` (`v0.0.4.5.10`) across all 22 host adapters, distribution records, manifests, and documentation surfaces.
- Preserved exactly five canonical public skills, four read-only public MCP tools, and zero em dashes across all files.

## [0.0.4.5.9] - 2026-10-08

### Added
- Repository Operating Vault: mandatory `.hypertaks/` local workspace with architecture pack (`ARCHITECTURE.md`, `FUNCTION-MAP.md`, `DATA-MODEL.md`, `NETWORK-DEPENDENCIES.md`, `ASSET-INDEX.md`) while preserving existing 13 Project Operating Context living documents.
- Repository Topological Scanner (RTS): multi-language AST and structural scanner for TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, and SQL with automated secret redaction.
- Local Intelligence Graph: first-party offline graph indexing (`nodes.jsonl`, `edges.jsonl`, `graph.json`, `graph.meta.json`, `GRAPH_REPORT.md`) with Git-aware freshness checking and impact/blast-radius analysis.
- Orchestrator V2: persistent run state under `.hypertaks/runs/<run-id>/`, topological DAG building, dependency waves, and interrupted run checkpointing and resume.
- Worker Governance: generic provider abstraction with Agency Agents provider, T6 untrusted evidence boundary, and anti-injection security containment.
- Local CLI: command surface (`init`, `status`, `sync`, `architecture`, `graph`) for repository vault operations.
- Security V2 & Behavioral Evals: 8 security regression tests and behavioral evaluations EV-91 through EV-112.
- Unified Capability Fabric: operational `execute()` dispatching across native, host, and MCP tools with honest status reporting, descriptor deduplication, and multilingual intent inference.
- Mandatory Repository Screening: Step 1e intake protocol with shallow and deep AST scanning profiles, dependency tracing, and coverage reporting.
- Layered Context Verification: 5-layer verification suite (STRUCTURAL, EVIDENCE, FRESHNESS, INTEGRITY, CONSISTENCY).
- Universal Context Generation: repository-agnostic `.ctx.md` documents preserving user customizations and marking unverified claims as UNKNOWN.
- Local Graph and Brain Reconciliation: cached graph rehydration avoiding redundant rebuilds.

### Changed
- Transitioned version identity to `0.0.4.5.9` (`v0.0.4.5.9`) with release single source of truth in `release/version.json`.
- Preserved exactly five public skills and four public MCP tools with zero em dashes across all files.

## [4.5.8] - 2026-09-20

### Added
- Embedded the Founder Anti-Slop Mandate (HATE AI SLOOP, HATE AI GENERIC, HATE AI LANGUAGE) into core skills, AGENTS.md, and workspace rules.
- Codified Subagent Model Tiering Protocol (1-2 tier downgrade rule, provider ladder mapping, and API key discovery habit).
- Codified Mandatory Visual Delivery (headless Agg Matplotlib, KaTeX, Mermaid/SVG, generate_image, tables).
- Resolved all 13 previously skipped eval cases to achieve 88/88 behavioral PASS under Boss-confirmed multi-host runtime harness.
- Established minimum graduation exam threshold of 80 (margin +8) in evaluation runner and rubric.

### Changed
